! Address modification by a NEGATIVE index value.
!
! HOW THIS WAS FOUND.  mutation_score.py replaced effAddr24's
!
!     return (x.sign == 1) ? (raw - x.addr) : (raw + x.addr);
!
! with an unconditional add -- dropping the index value's SIGN -- and it
! survived the whole suite.  effAddr24 is the address-modification
! helper behind every bit-addressed instruction in the model, so a
! survivor means one thing: not one program in 160+ ever indexes with a
! NEGATIVE value.  Index words with negative values exist all over the
! suite; none of them is used as a MODIFIER.
!
! NOT THE SAME GAP as branch_index_modified.strap.  That one closed
! effAddr19, the 19-bit half-word-address helper the branches use, and
! effAddr19 keeps its own copy of the sign test.  Closing one said
! nothing about the other -- two helpers, two tests.  This is the
! bit-address side, reached here through BRANCH ON BIT.
!
! THE RULE, Reference Manual p.20-21 "Address Modification": the SIGNED
! value field of the index register is added to the instruction's
! address field, and "the carry out of the top bit is ignored".
!
! THE SHAPE.  SCR's bit 0 is set, and the BZB addresses SCR2 -- one word
! ABOVE it -- modified by an index whose value is one word NEGATIVE, so
! the effective address comes back to SCR.  With the sign ignored the
! address runs the other way, to DUMMY, whose bit 0 is zero.  BZB
! branches when the bit is OFF, so the wrong address hangs and the right
! one falls through.  DUMMY exists only to be the wrong answer, and it
! must stay zero.
!
! WEAKER STANDARD, STATED: hand-written from p.20-21, not transcribed.

        SLC, (8)3300.0
START   BB1, SCR, $+1.0              ! set SCR bit 0 to one
        BZB, SCR, $                  ! hang up if that did not take
        LX, $1, WMINUSW              ! index value = one word, NEGATIVE
        BZB, SCR2($1), $             ! SCR2 - one word = SCR, whose bit is 1,
                                     !   so this must NOT branch.  With the
                                     !   sign ignored it addresses DUMMY,
                                     !   whose bit is 0, and hangs here.
        B, PASS
!
SCR     DD(BU,64), 0                 ! the right answer; bit 0 gets set
SCR2    DD(BU,64), 0                 ! the unmodified address
DUMMY   DD(BU,64), 0                 ! the wrong answer: must stay zero
WMINUSW XW, -(8)1.0, 0, 0, 0         ! value 64 bits = one word, sign 1
PASS    BEW, $
        END, START
